    "explanation": "The $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nWHY THE FEE CANNOT STAND. The trip was ended by the driver with the reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01 limb (d) accepts only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. That code is the driver's own statement that he could not find the rider, so limb (d) fails on the face of the trip record and the fee cannot be sustained under POL-NS-01. Independently, the GPS trace never places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius: his closest approach across all 92 fixes is 259.94 m, no qualifying in-radius fix exists, and the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 s against a 300 s minimum. Limb (b) and limb (c) of POL-NS-01 therefore fail as well, and POL-NS-02 returns the fee.\n\nPOL-NS-03 GIVES THE SAME RESULT AND SETTLES THE COST. The driver held position roughly 260 m from the Blk 118 pin — outside the arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling — for about the 384 seconds between his 07:26:40 arrival marker and his 07:33:05 cancellation. On those facts he did not arrive at the pickup point and the fee is refunded in full. As to who absorbs the loss, the chat log shows the rider naming the correct block ('im at blk 118') at 07:22:10, the driver answering 'ok coming' and reading it at 07:23:02, and the driver never moving to that block before cancelling. Under POL-NS-03(i) the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation. The pin-ambiguity goodwill in POL-NS-03(ii) does not apply: this trip registers a single pickup point, not two or more.\n\nDRIVER'S POINTS. Your account that the app pin pointed to the carpark side is noted, and your 6.4-minute wait is not disputed. But the record cannot establish that you waited at any particular other block or entrance: POL-NS-03 allows venue, block or entrance identity to rest only on a venue_id comparison or on a statement in the chat log, and neither supports it here — the rider's 'block 128' account appears in no artifact. Your 'arrived' marker is not a false marker under POL-NS-05: your closest approach stayed within that clause's 300 m leash and no in-motion fix is matched to the marker, so no false-arrival referral is entered. Your POL-NS-07 claim for 80% compensation (SGD 3.20) is declined: POL-NS-07 operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not, and POL-NS-03(i) independently gives no compensation on these facts. Your POL-NS-04 point is accepted — the driver did reply within 120 seconds, so that clause does not apply and the mislocation is decided under POL-NS-03.\n\nWEIGHT AND IMPAIRMENT. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00205) carries a schema-level impairment: weight 0.8, issue CONTENT_REDACTED. It is named here as POL-GEN-02(3) requires. The redaction removed only the unit number from the rider's first message; the block identifier the fault allocation turns on survives verbatim, so the finding survives the discount. The refund itself does not rest on the chat log — it rests on the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00205) and the trip record (EV-TRIP-00205), both at full weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and the ruling is comfortably above the 0.70 floor. The chat does not meet any limb (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08: no clock skew, a complete 100%-coverage trace, no chat sequence gap or hole across the arrival marker, and the $4.00 line reconciles with STANDARD + RYDE_X.\n\nNO ESCALATION. Both disputes_with_counterparty_90d figures are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) cannot fire; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the POL-NS-09(d) threshold of 3; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations against 104 completed trips, a rate of 0.019); no two admissible artifacts contradict each other in a way no clause resolves; and the deciding evidence is not impaired under POL-NS-08. The case is decided rather than parked.\n\nAMOUNT. The cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.00 is refunded in full. No driver compensation is payable."
  },
